## 1. How a team with cells works

{{ team.label }} is split into cells under its flight commander: {% for c in team.cells %}{{ c.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. The rules are the same as for any team ({% if rules == "full" %}Player Rules Handbook §2.10{% else %}Basic Rules §5.4{% endif %}):

- **One COA per team.** Your cell doesn't make its own COA. You **propose** the COA you think matters most, with its Pros, and the flight commander chooses **one** for the whole team. A COA may use counters from any cell.
- **Requests are shared.** The team has {{ requests }} RFIs and RFFs a turn in total ({{ planning_requests }} in Phase I), not {{ requests }} for each cell. Agree with the other cells whose requests go first.
- **Brief what the commander chose.** Once the commander decides, the whole team argues for that COA, including the cells whose idea lost.
- **Bring disagreements to the commander early**, in Prepare, not in your COA slot. In the slot, the team speaks with one voice.

